  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 RNA encoder with multiprofile + transformer aggregation is clearly the dominant architecture (0.725 acc for config_040, 0.721 for config_008), far outperforming scgpt (~0.52) and singleprofile (~0.42). Fusion method (weighted vs concat) shows negligible difference (~0.4%). The key untested variable for this top-performing RNA encoder is the image encoder: all top configs use imagenet_vit_l, but resnet50 has never been paired with scvi_n200. This experiment (config_048: scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted) isolates the image-encoder choice while holding all other parameters at their best-known values. It clarifies whether the image modality's contribution is architecture-dependent and whether a different visual backbone could complement the RNA features to push accuracy above 0.725. Under the 4-remaining-experiment budget, this is the highest-information test: if resnet50 matches or beats ViT-L, we gain a cheaper image pathway; if it underperforms, we confirm ViT-L is optimal and can focus remaining budget on finer tuning. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-low (~2.5–3.0 GPU hours), since ResNet-50 is substantially smaller than ViT-Large, making this cheaper than config_040 (3.60 hrs) while maintaining the same transformer aggregation and fusion pipeline."
}

